  "help.basicsBody": "Encrypt: Go to the Encrypt tab, choose the files or folders you want to encrypt (multiple selection is supported), enter a password, and press Encrypt.\n\nDecrypt: Two ways — double-click the .locked marker file left at the original location, or find the item in the Encrypted Items tab and use its unlock button.\n\nEncrypted Items: View all currently encrypted items, decrypt them individually, permanently delete them, and see the full activity history.",
  "help.howItWorksTitle": "How It Works",
  "help.howItWorksBody": "After encryption, the content is moved to a centralized storage location (the Vault). Only a marker file named .locked is left at the original location — it contains no original content, and simply marks that something used to be there.\n\nThere are three independent unlock methods that can be enabled together: password (always required; the other two are optional extras), Passkey (quick unlock using this device's Windows Hello), and recovery key (a one-time-displayed backup code).\n\nThe Vault location can be changed in Settings to a cloud sync folder (e.g. OneDrive), letting multiple devices share the encrypted content through your sync client for cross-device backup — but the password itself is never synced; you need to remember it yourself.",
